 "mf.ai.1.h": "A supporting view",
 "mf.ai.1.p": "Customers found the donut chart's percentage hard to read, so I built a helper view that puts a bin-shaped 2D drawing next to the camera photo, shipped first to two farms on web and app. Web and app compute the value separately and can disagree, so moving the calculation to the server is the next step.",
 "mf.ai.2.h": "Discarded images back into training",
 "mf.ai.2.p": "Proposed having people re-label, as masks, the images the model failed to segment so they could be used for retraining, and built the labelling screen: a Canvas editor for circles and polygons, coordinates normalised to 0–1 regardless of image size, and status badges after a retraining request. The labelled images were used in retraining; the model now sorts these cases itself, so the step is no longer used.",
 "mf.ai.label": "AI result screens",
 "mf.ai.title": "What the AI produces,<br>made judgeable by people.",
 "mf.limit.1": "Notification request counts come from the change commits and are in production; monitoring-screen requests (98→50) were measured on staging. None of this measures perceived speed for every user.",
 "mf.limit.2": "The helper view is live on two farms so far. It does not make the fill-level estimate more accurate.",
 "mf.limit.3": "It is an internal service, so there is no public link.",
 "mf.limit.4": "Screens were captured with test accounts and contain no real farm data.",
 "mf.limit.h": "About the numbers and scope",
 "mf.me.p": "Monitoring screens, admin and web notifications, the permission layer, fewer requests, shared UI clean-up, language packs, and the labelling screen for retraining.",
 "mf.nt.a.h": "Pauses when nobody is looking",
