 "mf.nt.a.p": "Cut each poll from six requests to one, and stopped it in hidden tabs.",
 "mf.nt.b.h": "Keeps running in hidden tabs",
 "mf.nt.b.label": "Covering dropped push notifications",
 "mf.nt.b.p": "I narrowed down notifications not showing on one browser by comparing it with others, and left this check running.",
 "mf.nt.cap2": "Per-bin notification settings",
 "mf.nt.case.1.h": "Symptom",
 "mf.nt.case.1.p": "On Edge 151, web pushes never reached the service worker, so no notification appeared (August 2026).",
 "mf.nt.case.2.h": "Comparison",
 "mf.nt.case.2.p": "The same notification showed in other browsers, which narrowed it to the browser rather than the server.",
 "mf.nt.case.3.h": "Call",
 "mf.nt.case.3.p": "Rather than dig into the browser internals, I first made sure the notification reached the user.",
 "mf.nt.case.4.h": "Fix",
 "mf.nt.case.4.p": "When polling finds more unread items, a visible tab gets an in-page toast and a hidden tab an OS notification. The same tag and a record of shown IDs keep push and polling from showing it twice.",
 "mf.nt.case.5.h": "Limits",
