 "mf.sub": "My Feed is a feed-management web service used by some 130 farms as of July 2026. I handle its web development and operation, building and fixing the farm monitoring screens, the admin and the web notifications.",
 "mf.title": "Farm screens,<br>lighter and easier to read.",
 "mf.ui.1.h": "Menus that are easy to find",
 "mf.ui.1.p": "Customer enquiries showed people struggled to find menus, so I reworked the paths to the main tasks and made the screens easier to read.",
 "mf.ui.2.h": "Shared UI fixed in one place",
 "mf.ui.2.p": "Consolidated shared UI that had been copied across pages, so it can be changed in one place.",
 "mf.ui.3.h": "Text as per-language keys",
 "mf.ui.3.p": "Moved screen text to per-language key–value packs, replacing a flow that waited on a translation API.",
 "mf.ui.4.h": "Table columns per account",
 "mf.ui.4.p": "Company, dealer and farm accounts need different columns, so permission classes decide which ones show, and below 1350px only the key columns stay. Long scrolling tables became pages.",
 "mf.ui.5.h": "Matching list and detail order",
 "mf.ui.5.p": "The list's sort order and the detail screen's arrow navigation disagreed. When re-sorting in the API didn't fix it, I passed the order actually rendered on screen through browser storage so the detail screen follows it.",
 "mf.ui.6.h": "Flickering tooltip images",
 "mf.ui.6.p": "Chart tooltips swapped images in immediately; loading them first and swapping afterwards removed the flicker.",
 "mf.ui.7.h": "Faulty-device report in one go",
 "mf.ui.7.p": "An AI-browser attempt to collect per-farm device faults stalled on large accounts, so I switched to pulling the admin APIs in parallel and downloading an Excel report directly.",
 "mf.ui.label": "Screen fixes",
 "mf.ui.title": "Start from the enquiry,<br>finish on the screen.",
